{title: Only Trust Him (Come, Every Soul by Sin Oppressed)}
{artist: John H. Stockton}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 113}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Baptist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Convention Press, 1975), # 183)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Come, every soul by sin oppressed;
[G]There’s mercy with the [D]Lord,
[G]And He will surely [C]give you rest
[G]By trusting [D7]in His [G]Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Only trust Him, [C]only [G]trust Him,
[G]Only trust Him [D]now;
[G]He will save you, [C]He will [G]save you,
[G]He will [D7]save you [G]now.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]For Jesus shed His precious blood
[G]Rich blessings to be[D]stow;
[G]Plunge now into the [C]crimson flood
[G]That washes [D7]white as [G]snow.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Yes, Jesus is the truth, the way,
[G]That leads you into [D]rest;
[G]Believe in Him with[C]out delay
[G]And you are [D7]fully [G]blessed.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Come, then, and join this holy band,
[G]And on to glory [D]go
[G]To dwell in that ce[C]lestial land
[G]Where joys im[D7]mortal [G]flow.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]O Jesus, blessèd Jesus, dear,
[G]I’m coming now to [D]Thee;
[G]Since Thou hast made the [C]way so clear
[G]And full sal[D7]vation [G]free.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
